  E084: [
    ["The regulator fixes the total quantity of pollution and issues permits, which firms may trade.", "The regulator fixes the total catch of fish and issues fishing quotas, which firms may trade."],
    ["Supply of permits is VERTICAL - total pollution is capped with certainty, which a tax cannot guarantee.", "The supply of quotas is vertical because the total catch is capped with certainty, which a tax cannot guarantee."],
    ["Firms that can abate cheaply do so and sell their spare permits; firms that cannot, buy. Abatement therefore happens where it is cheapest, which is cost-efficient.", "Firms that can cut their catch cheaply do so and sell their spare quotas, and firms that cannot, buy. The catch therefore falls where it is cheapest to cut, which is cost-efficient."],
    ["Tightening the cap over time raises the permit price and strengthens the incentive to invest in clean technology.", "Tightening the cap over time raises the quota price and strengthens the incentive to invest in selective gear and sustainable methods."],
    ["The market discovers the price, so the regulator does not need to know the cost of abatement.", "The market discovers the price, so the regulator does not need to know the cost of cutting the catch."],
    ["A tax on spending, used to internalise a negative externality by raising private cost to social cost.", "A tax on each unit of fish landed, used to internalise a negative externality by raising private cost to social cost."],
    ["A payment to producers to lower costs, used to correct under-consumption of a merit good or a positive externality.", "A payment to producers to lower costs, which could fund sustainable gear or fish farming so that less pressure falls on wild stocks."],
    ["Supply shifts right by the amount of the subsidy per unit, so price to the consumer falls and quantity rises towards Q*.", "Supply of farmed or sustainably caught fish shifts right by the amount of the subsidy per unit, so the price falls and demand switches away from over-fished wild stocks."],
  ],
